    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.starter\r\n\r\n### Question\r\n\r\nHi echasnovski! \r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/76fff636-2cde-46bf-9bdb-4410fec608cb)\r\nSo above is the image of my mini.starter. The issue I am actually facing is that there is a grey strip which appears on the left of the the mini.starter which is nothing but statuscolumn. So, setting statuscolumn like this ``set statuscolumn=`` removes it completely.\r\n\r\nNow I had two questions here :- \r\n1. How do I do this programatically in neovim lua as I use the following plugin for statuscolumn configuration and adding ministarter to ft_ignore does not remove it?\r\n```lua\r\nadd(\"luukvbaal/statuscol.nvim\")\r\n        require(\"statuscol\").setup({\r\n                relculright = false,\r\n                bt_ignore = { \"terminal\", \"\\\\[dap-repl-*\\\\]\" },\r\n                ft_ignore = { \"ministarter\", \"help\" },\r\n                segments = {\r\n                        { text = { \"%s\" }, click = \"v:lua.ScSa\" },\r\n                        {\r\n                                text = { require(\"statuscol.builtin\").lnumfunc },\r\n                                click = \"v:lua.ScLa\",\r\n                        },\r\n                        {\r\n                                text = { require(\"statuscol.builtin\").foldfunc, \" \" },\r\n                                click = \"v:lua.ScFa\",\r\n                        },\r\n                },\r\n        })\r\n```\r\n3. Does it actually make sense to do this setting statuscolumn to empty thing from mini.starter plugin itself since there is no need to have statuscolumn shown in the first place in mini.starter screen?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.starter</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hi echasnovski!<br>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/56352048/402871848-76fff636-2cde-46bf-9bdb-4410fec608cb.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..jtjooTX4oQ2L5vg4wbBQ_BhGlfTXzd1e4yoCoCZ-dac\"><img src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/56352048/402871848-76fff636-2cde-46bf-9bdb-4410fec608cb.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..jtjooTX4oQ2L5vg4wbBQ_BhGlfTXzd1e4yoCoCZ-dac\" alt=\"image\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a><br>\nSo above is the image of my mini.starter. The issue I am actually facing is that there is a grey strip which appears on the left of the the mini.starter which is nothing but statuscolumn. So, setting statuscolumn like this <code class=\"notranslate\">set statuscolumn=</code> removes it completely.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Now I had two questions here :-</p>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>How do I do this programatically in neovim lua as I use the following plugin for statuscolumn configuration and adding ministarter to ft_ignore does not remove it?</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"add(&quot;luukvbaal/statuscol.nvim&quot;)\n        require(&quot;statuscol&quot;).setup({\n                relculright = false,\n                bt_ignore = { &quot;terminal&quot;, &quot;\\\\[dap-repl-*\\\\]&quot; },\n                ft_ignore = { &quot;ministarter&quot;, &quot;help&quot; },\n                segments = {\n                        { text = { &quot;%s&quot; }, click = &quot;v:lua.ScSa&quot; },\n                        {\n                                text = { require(&quot;statuscol.builtin&quot;).lnumfunc },\n                                click = &quot;v:lua.ScLa&quot;,\n                        },\n                        {\n                                text = { require(&quot;statuscol.builtin&quot;).foldfunc, &quot; &quot; },\n                                click = &quot;v:lua.ScFa&quot;,\n                        },\n                },\n        })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">add</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>luukvbaal/statuscol.nvim<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>)\n        <span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>statuscol<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n                <span class=\"pl-smi\">relculright</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span>,\n                <span class=\"pl-smi\">bt_ignore</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>terminal<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span><span class=\"pl-cce\">\\\\</span>[dap-repl-*<span class=\"pl-cce\">\\\\</span>]<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>},\n                <span class=\"pl-smi\">ft_ignore</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>ministarter<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>help<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>},\n                <span class=\"pl-smi\">segments</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n                        { <span class=\"pl-smi\">text</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>%s<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>}, <span class=\"pl-smi\">click</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>v:lua.ScSa<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>},\n                        {\n                                <span class=\"pl-smi\">text</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>statuscol.builtin<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-e\">lnumfunc</span> },\n                                <span class=\"pl-smi\">click</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>v:lua.ScLa<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>,\n                        },\n                        {\n                                <span class=\"pl-smi\">text</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>statuscol.builtin<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-e\">foldfunc</span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span> <span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>},\n                                <span class=\"pl-smi\">click</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>v:lua.ScFa<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>,\n                        },\n                },\n        })</pre></div>\n<ol start=\"3\" dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Does it actually make sense to do this setting statuscolumn to empty thing from mini.starter plugin itself since there is no need to have statuscolumn shown in the first place in mini.starter screen?</li>\n</ol>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.starter\nQuestion\nHi echasnovski!\n\nSo above is the image of my mini.starter. The issue I am actually facing is that there is a grey strip which appears on the left of the the mini.starter which is nothing but statuscolumn. So, setting statuscolumn like this set statuscolumn= removes it completely.\nNow I had two questions here :-\n\nHow do I do this programatically in neovim lua as I use the following plugin for statuscolumn configuration and adding ministarter to ft_ignore does not remove it?\n\nadd(\"luukvbaal/statuscol.nvim\")\n        require(\"statuscol\").setup({\n                relculright = false,\n                bt_ignore = { \"terminal\", \"\\\\[dap-repl-*\\\\]\" },\n                ft_ignore = { \"ministarter\", \"help\" },\n                segments = {\n                        { text = { \"%s\" }, click = \"v:lua.ScSa\" },\n                        {\n                                text = { require(\"statuscol.builtin\").lnumfunc },\n                                click = \"v:lua.ScLa\",\n                        },\n                        {\n                                text = { require(\"statuscol.builtin\").foldfunc, \" \" },\n                                click = \"v:lua.ScFa\",\n                        },\n                },\n        })\n\nDoes it actually make sense to do this setting statuscolumn to empty thing from mini.starter plugin itself since there is no need to have statuscolumn shown in the first place in mini.starter screen?",
