            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": ">     1. How do I do this programatically in neovim lua as I use the following plugin for statuscolumn configuration and adding ministarter to ft_ignore does not remove it?\r\n\r\nUse [dedicated event](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/3d81b8ab6ad4b805c2e7b42f2e93e3dbb68dd12a/doc/mini-starter.txt#L263-L265) to set the option locally. There is no `FileType` event triggered for 'ministarter' filetype for performance reasons (which is crucial as 'mini.starter' is loaded/executed during startup).\r\n\r\n>     3. Does it actually make sense to do this setting statuscolumn to empty thing from mini.starter plugin itself since there is no need to have statuscolumn shown in the first place in mini.starter screen?\r\n\r\nYeah, it indeed might be a good idea. I was hesitant previously because it was a relatively new feature and 'mini.nvim' still supports Neovim 0.8 which doesn't have it implemented.",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"1. How do I do this programatically in neovim lua as I use the following plugin for statuscolumn configuration and adding ministarter to ft_ignore does not remove it?\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">1. How do I do this programatically in neovim lua as I use the following plugin for statuscolumn configuration and adding ministarter to ft_ignore does not remove it?\n</code></pre></div>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Use <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/3d81b8ab6ad4b805c2e7b42f2e93e3dbb68dd12a/doc/mini-starter.txt#L263-L265\">dedicated event</a> to set the option locally. There is no <code class=\"notranslate\">FileType</code> event triggered for 'ministarter' filetype for performance reasons (which is crucial as 'mini.starter' is loaded/executed during startup).</p>\n<blockquote>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"3. Does it actually make sense to do this setting statuscolumn to empty thing from mini.starter plugin itself since there is no need to have statuscolumn shown in the first place in mini.starter screen?\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">3. Does it actually make sense to do this setting statuscolumn to empty thing from mini.starter plugin itself since there is no need to have statuscolumn shown in the first place in mini.starter screen?\n</code></pre></div>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Yeah, it indeed might be a good idea. I was hesitant previously because it was a relatively new feature and 'mini.nvim' still supports Neovim 0.8 which doesn't have it implemented.</p>",
            "bodyText": "1. How do I do this programatically in neovim lua as I use the following plugin for statuscolumn configuration and adding ministarter to ft_ignore does not remove it?\n\n\nUse dedicated event to set the option locally. There is no FileType event triggered for 'ministarter' filetype for performance reasons (which is crucial as 'mini.starter' is loaded/executed during startup).\n\n3. Does it actually make sense to do this setting statuscolumn to empty thing from mini.starter plugin itself since there is no need to have statuscolumn shown in the first place in mini.starter screen?\n\n\nYeah, it indeed might be a good idea. I was hesitant previously because it was a relatively new feature and 'mini.nvim' still supports Neovim 0.8 which doesn't have it implemented.",
